[[:db/cas :question-weights/activity-type :db/doc "Activity-type enum selecting the distribution's use, initially activity.type/lesson or activity.type/review. Reuses the enums defined in content/0-activity.edn." "Activity-type enum selecting the distribution's use: activity.type/lesson, activity.type/review, or activity.type/assessment. Reuses the enums defined in content/0-activity.edn."] [:db/cas :question-weights/validate :db/doc "Requires an activity type and all six weights when explicitly ensured. The application checks allowed activity types, finite nonnegative weights, a positive finite total for each distribution, exactly one policy owner, and one record per activity type in that policy. Weights are normalized across eligible bands before selecting a fresh question within the chosen band; an unavailable question supply is not learner failure. Stopping rules remain application code." "Requires an activity type and all six weights when explicitly ensured. The application supports lessons, reviews, and assessments and checks finite nonnegative weights, a positive finite total for each distribution, exactly one policy owner, and one record per activity type in that policy. Lessons and reviews choose the phase using their stopping rules; ordinary assessments use initial weights throughout, while a designated assessment retake/recheck explicitly requests remedial weights. Weights are normalized across eligible bands before selecting a fresh question within the chosen band; an unavailable question supply is not learner failure. Stopping rules and retake scheduling remain application code."] {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409231 :policy/question-selection-weights [{:db/id "assessment-weights" :question-weights/activity-type :activity.type/assessment :question-weights/initial-easy 50.0 :question-weights/initial-moderate 40.0 :question-weights/initial-hard 10.0 :question-weights/remedial-easy 45.0 :question-weights/remedial-moderate 40.0 :question-weights/remedial-hard 15.0 :db/ensure :question-weights/validate}] :db/ensure :policy/validate}]
